{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fe864acfaaefe923c5d2d4ed76b71d0df7bd6d3a9a0229c80ad5aa7846b0d0b5","digest":{"component_or_area":"scripts/ module import resolution","key_entities":["scripts/canary_bridge.py:26","scripts/dependency_audit.py:50","alert_dedup","sys.path.insert","__file__","tests/unit/test_reconcile_bridge_canary_class.py","tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py"],"problem_keywords":["module resolution","sys.path","bare import","subset test failure","import precedent"],"propositions":["Bare import of alert_dedup in canary_bridge.py and dependency_audit.py resolves only when scripts/ is on sys.path, causing ModuleNotFoundError when test files are run as subsets outside CI.","CI full test suite passes because conftest.py inserts scripts/ on sys.path at collection time, masking the failure in standalone test runs that developers do during iteration.","The fix applies explicit invocation-independent sys.path.insert derived from __file__ above each bare sibling-module import, following the precedent pattern in jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py.","A new guard test test_scripts_import_convention.py AST-scans for unprotected bare imports under scripts/ and runs a subprocess check that affected test modules collect when executed alone."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787901281205863001,"uuid":"45a517ce-4053-4807-b09a-0f5ae2bd5a02"}